        "eyebrow": "Virtual staging near you",
        "heading": "Virtual Staging Tampa, FL",
        "lede": "Virtual staging means furnishing the listing photos rather than the house: a designer adds 3D furniture, artwork and decor to images of empty or cleared rooms so potential buyers can picture living there, with nothing delivered to the property. Tampa Bay is one of America's busiest relocation markets, shopped largely from out of state, and Bella's designers stage Tampa listings in 24 to 48 hours, from {price:virtual-staging} a photo.",
        "cta_label": "Stage my listing — from {price:virtual-staging}",
        "cta_link": "/products/virtual-staging",
        "alt_label": "Browse the lookbook",
        "alt_link": "/pages/lookbook",
        "city": "Tampa",
        "market_heading": "Why virtual staging matters in the Tampa market",
        "market_text": "<p>Tampa Bay has spent years near the top of national relocation lists, and the buyers arriving from the Northeast and Midwest do most of their shopping before the moving truck is booked. For them the listing photos are the property tour — and an empty stucco ranch with tile floors reads as an echo, not a home.</p><p>The bay itself does heavy lifting in local marketing: staged waterfront lanais, pool decks and bonus rooms consistently out-perform interior shots. Our home staging covers outdoor living too, and day-to-dusk editing turns a flat exterior into the sunset-over-the-water shot.</p><p>Tampa's inventory also skews toward the two hardest room types to photograph empty: wide-open great rooms in newer builds, where there's nothing to establish scale, and tiled Florida rooms that read as unfinished space until furniture gives them a purpose.</p><p>For those buyers the photos decide the shortlist: 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors. Staged homes give potential buyers the scale, color and warmth an empty room can't — and the confidence to book a flight for the showing.</p><p>Empty rooms tend to look smaller and less inviting in listing photos. Virtual staging is a cost-effective way to market a vacant Tampa home: it makes cold rooms feel lived-in, shows room dimensions and layout at a glance, and highlights key features, flow and lifestyle spaces like the lanai — with a faster turnaround than physical staging services.</p>",
        "local_heading": "Home staging, Tampa Bay style — done virtually",
        "local_text": "<p>Designers stage coastal-transitional for waterfront and beach communities, clean contemporary for downtown and Water Street condos, and family looks for Carrollwood, Westchase and the Pasco and Hillsborough suburbs. Files are Stellar MLS-ready in 24 to 48 hours.</p><p>Outdoor rooms are staged as rooms. A screened lanai or pool deck with furniture in it does more for a Tampa listing than another angle of the same living room.</p><p>Homeowners, investors and agents order the same way: place the order, upload your photos and your designer handles the furnishings, lamps and artwork. Every image comes with disclosure guidance and full usage rights, and volume discounts apply automatically — 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+ — which keeps whole-home sets within budget.</p>",
        "hoods_label": "Where we stage most",
        "hoods": "South Tampa, Hyde Park, Seminole Heights, Water Street, Westchase, Carrollwood, St. Petersburg, Clearwater, Riverview"
      }
    },
