        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you stage a screened lanai or pool deck?",
            "answer": "Yes, and in Tampa we'd recommend it before another interior angle. Outdoor living is a large part of what buyers are shopping for, and an empty lanai is one of the weakest photos in a typical listing set."
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "My buyers are relocating from up north and haven't visited. Does staging help?",
            "answer": "It's most of what they're judging on. A buyer building a shortlist from Ohio or New Jersey has only the photos, and an empty tiled room gives them no sense of scale or of what living there feels like."
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "The great room is huge and empty. How do you handle that?",
            "answer": "By establishing scale. Wide-open great rooms are hard to read without furniture — there's nothing to measure against. Staged with a seating arrangement and a dining zone, the same room reads as generous rather than cavernous."
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much does it cost to stage a house in Florida?",
            "answer": "Physical staging in Florida is quoted per home — the size of the house, the number of rooms and the rental length all move the price. As a general benchmark, conventional staging runs about $2,000–5,000 a month until the home sells. Virtual staging from Bella is {price:virtual-staging} a photo, paid once, with no rental to extend if the listing sits."
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How much do people charge for virtual staging?",
            "answer": "Prices vary by provider and by whether a person or an AI app does the work. Bella's designer-made virtual staging is {price:virtual-staging} per photo, with volume discounts of 5% at 3+ photos, 10% at 6+, 15% at 11+ and 20% at 21+. Furniture removal for occupied rooms, unlimited revisions for two weeks and full usage rights are included — no subscription, no minimum."
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging worth it?",
            "answer": "For most vacant or dated listings, yes. Staging can't guarantee a sale, but 97% of buyers use the internet in their home search, according to the National Association of Realtors, so the photos decide which homes get a showing. NAR's research on home staging also finds that staging makes it easier for buyers to visualize a property as their future home. For a Tampa buyer shopping from out of state, virtually staged photos are often the whole first impression: well-staged images capture attention quickly and can lift online engagement with the listing, for a one-time cost per photo instead of monthly furniture rental."
          }
        },
        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in Florida?",
            "answer": "Yes — virtual staging is a standard marketing practice as long as it doesn't misrepresent the property, and real estate professionals should disclose it in the listing. Add furniture and decor only, don't hide defects or change permanent features, and disclose that the photos are virtually staged; the NAR Code of Ethics requires a true picture in advertising. Check Stellar MLS rules for exact labeling. Every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
        },
        "q9": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can you show a room in more than one style, or a home that isn't built yet?",
            "answer": "Yes. Because the furniture is digital, a room can be staged in more than one Look Book style, which makes it easy to test which look suits the buyer. For dated rooms, virtual renovation (from {price:virtual-renovation-service}) shows new floors, walls and finishes; for homes that aren't built yet, 3D rendering (from {price:3d-rendering}) creates photorealistic images from plans."
          }
        },
        "q10": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How can I virtually stage my home for free?",
            "answer": "Free AI apps and DIY software can drop furniture into a photo, but the results often distort scale and finishes, and a misleading image creates disclosure problems. New clients can claim a $40 voucher on Bella's sign-up page to try designer-made staging, subject to Bella's approval."
          }
        },
        "q11": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How does virtual staging compare with Tampa home stagers?",
            "answer": "Tampa home stagers bring real furniture, which helps at in-person showings but means a monthly rental and a schedule to work around. Virtual staging changes only the photos: {price:virtual-staging} a photo, back in 24 to 48 hours. It suits the online listing, where most buyers first see the home."
          }
        }
